# Safety and privacy

Use fixture data for tests and local runs.

Never commit secrets, keys, `nsec`s, or `.env` files. Commit config templates only, such as `.env.example`.

Ask before destructive git (`reset --hard`, `clean`, force-push, rebase of shared history). One exception: `--force-with-lease` of your own unmerged `cursor/*` branch after a red-review change request ([`tdd.mdc`](tdd.mdc)).

Never push to `main`, including a force-push.
